# Canonical list of the promotion-ring channels, most-stable first, one per line. This file is
# the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the three rings nexus-flow promotes through (nexus-flow-85y.27).
# The ring was duplicated across crates/cli/src/selfupdate.rs (the `CHANNELS` array), the clap
# `--channel` value_parser in crates/cli/src/lib.rs and install.sh's `NXF_CHANNEL` doc comment;
# `cargo xtask channels check` (a CI gate) now asserts every one of those copies agrees with this
# file, so adding/renaming a ring is a single edit here followed by a failing check that names
# every consumer still to update. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# ONE CONSUMER IS OUT OF REACH AND IS NOT CHECKED (nexus-flow-6j6v.sgfr). The updater Lambda's
# download-path regex `download/(stable|beta|alpha)/…` used to be checked here as
# `infra/lambda/updater/decide.ts`; that tree moved to nxsflow-landing-page with the delivery
# migration, and the copy this check kept reading was a leftover nobody deployed. See the same
# paragraph in `release/platforms` — a renamed or added ring must be carried into the landing
# repo's updater by hand, and the failure mode is a silent "no update available" on that ring.
stable
beta
alpha
